{"name":"Backlight","hex":"#fcf0e5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"backlight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Light shining from a source behind the object of interest or attention.","A spotlight that illuminates a photographic subject from behind."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To illuminate something from behind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Backlight","blocks":[{"text":"A backlight is a form of illumination used in liquid-crystal displays (LCDs) that provides light from the back or side of a display panel. LCDs do not produce light on their own, so they require illumination—either from ambient light or a dedicated light source—to create a visible image. Backlights are commonly used in smartphones, computer monitors, and LCD televisions. They are also used in small displays, such as wristwatches, to enhance readability in low-light conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Backlit_LCD_display.jpg/330px-Backlit_LCD_display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backlight"},{"title":"Backlight (TV program)","blocks":[{"text":"Backlight is a documentary television program by Dutch public broadcasting organisation VPRO. The first episode of Backlight was broadcast on 8 September 2002."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/97/VPRO_Backlight_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backlight_(TV_program)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg/500px-LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg/1280px-LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg/500px-LCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" 18 parallel CCFLs as backlight for an LCD TV","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALCD-TV_Backlight_with_CCFL.jpg"}],"sounds":{"backlight":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-backlight.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-backlight.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-backlight.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-backlight.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-backlight.wav.ogg"}]}}}